--TEST--
`as ?T` is refused at both ends of its table — a row that cannot fail, and a pair naming no row at all — `rule:expressions/nullable-conversion-availability`, over `rule:types/conversion`'s closed table
--FILE--
<?nvs
// `rule:expressions/nullable-conversion-availability` in one sentence: "a conversion that exists and failed is
// `null`; a conversion that does not exist is a diagnostic" — and a
// conversion that *cannot fail* is a diagnostic too, because the `?` then
// promises a `null` no run produces and every reader after it has to check
// for it. The plain `as T` form is refused at one end only, so the sugar
// takes one refusal of its own and shares the other.
enum Mode { Read, Write }

class Helper {
    public static function nothing(): void {}
}

class Foo { public int $n = 1; }

array<int> $xs = [1, 2];
bool $flag = true;
int $i = 7;
string $s = "abc";
Mode $mode = Mode::Read;
Mode::Read $read = Mode::Read;
Foo $foo = new Foo();

// End one, and the sugar's alone: a row that always succeeds. `as ?T` "yields
// `null` exactly where `as T` would throw", so over these it yields it
// nowhere. Each help names `as T`.
?int $a = $i as ?int;
?string $b = $i as ?string;
?bool $c = $xs as ?bool;
?int $d = $mode as ?int;
?mixed $e = $s as ?mixed;
?Mode $f = $read as ?Mode;

// End two, shared with the plain form: `rule:types/conversion`'s table is closed, and
// asking it through the sugar asks it of the `T` inside. Every pair here is
// one `the-conversion-table-is-closed` already pins without the `?`.
?int $g = $xs as ?int;
?float $h = $mode as ?float;
?int $j = $flag as ?int;
?bytes $k = $i as ?bytes;
?array<int> $l = $s as ?array<int>;
?string $m = Helper::nothing() as ?string;
?int $n = null as ?int;

// § 3's third refusal, absolute and with a help of its own: `as?` spells a
// downcast in every language a reader arrives from, and no class is a row.
?Foo $o = $foo as ?Foo;
--EXPECT--

--EXPECTF-ERROR--
error[E0709]: `int as ?int` cannot fail, so it never answers `null`
%A
error[E0709]: `int as ?string` cannot fail, so it never answers `null`
%A
error[E0709]: `array<int> as ?bool` cannot fail, so it never answers `null`
%A
error[E0709]: `Mode as ?int` cannot fail, so it never answers `null`
%A
error[E0709]: `string as ?mixed` cannot fail, so it never answers `null`
%A
error[E0709]: `Mode::Read as ?Mode` cannot fail, so it never answers `null`
%A
error[E0708]: `array<int>` cannot be converted to `int`
%A
error[E0708]: `Mode` cannot be converted to `float`
%A
error[E0708]: `bool` cannot be converted to `int`
%A
error[E0708]: `int` cannot be converted to `bytes`
%A
error[E0708]: `string` cannot be converted to `array<int>`
%A
error[E0708]: `void` cannot be converted to `string`
%A
error[E0708]: `null` cannot be converted to `int`
%A
error[E0473]: `Foo` is a class, so `as ?Foo` is not a conversion
%A
